WHY cordis.patch.yml LOOKS UNCHANGED (and that is correct)
  cordis.yml states the tree is composed as patches: first every bundle in package.json's
  dsh.profile.bundles, then cordis.patch.yml, then --patch overlays. Because the plugin was enabled as a
  BUNDLE, its configuration comes from the plugin's own cordis.patch.yml inside the package, and the
  profile-level file only needs entries for things the profile overrides. So its absence there is
  expected, not a sign that it was left disabled.

THE COMPATIBILITY GATE WAS PASSED
  .plugin-manager\logs\operation-mWh9Hd\pnpm.log records a clean install:
      dependencies: + dsh-guard-repeat-output ^2.1.7 / Packages: +1 / Done in 766ms
  By contrast another operation was refused outright:
