HOW TO CONFIRM IT IS ACTUALLY WORKING LATER
  The plugin writes two artifacts under %USERPROFILE%\.dsh\logs\ :
    dsh-guard-repeat-output.log        - one record per conviction (nothing yet: no collapse happened)
    guard-repeat-output-pruned\        - sidecar copies of discarded text (up to 262144 chars each)
  Either file appearing IS the proof that it intercepted something. Until then it is armed but untested.

TWO MISTAKES I MADE WHILE BUILDING THE VERIFICATION SCRIPT (both are now documented rules)
  1. Wrote the script as UTF-8 WITHOUT BOM. PowerShell 5.1 read the Chinese comments as GB2312, the
     mojibake broke the parse, and it died with "Unexpected token". This is exactly the failure already
     recorded in AGENTS.md rule 0 - I walked into it again one hour after writing the rule, which is
     decent evidence that the rule is worth having. Fixed by writing with UTF8Encoding($true).
  2. Named a parameter $Home, which collides with PowerShell's read-only automatic variable:
     "Cannot overwrite variable Home because it is read-only or constant."
     Renamed to $DshHome. (Same class of mistake as the earlier $HOME note in the rules.)

TUNABLES, IF IT EVER MISFIRES
  Edit the plugin's own config in the Plugins page (written into the profile patch; usually no restart):
    truncateChannels   default ['reasoning']  - only the reasoning channel is cut
    modelIncludes      default ['deepseek']   - restrict to DeepSeek-family models
    maxDegenerationRetries default 2          - discard-and-reissue budget
    windowChars / minSegments / phraseRun / lowInfoDupShare / maxUniqueGramRatio - detection sensitivity
    copyDir / copyMaxChars                    - sidecar copies (set copyDir null to disable)
    logPath                                   - conviction log location